M-Pesa Daraja Gateway (C2B & B2C Node.js / TypeScript Integration)

A production-ready, highly secure full-stack M-Pesa payment gateway built with Node.js, Express.js, TypeScript, and MongoDB (Mongoose). This service handles both Customer-to-Business (C2B / STK Push) transactions and Business-to-Customer (B2C / Bulk Disbursement) payouts with built-in asynchronous reconciliation, webhook dispatchers, rate-limiting protection, and RSA credential security.
🚀 Core Features & Architecture
1. Customer-to-Business (C2B / STK Push)

    Initiation: Generates cryptographically secure timestamps and passwords (Buffer.from(Shortcode + Passkey + Timestamp).toString("base64")) to trigger STK Push requests.

    Authentication: Automated OAuth token retrieval with custom Incapsula firewall user-agent and header evasion safeguards.

    Callbacks: Secure webhook receivers (/api/v1/mpesa/callback) handling successful payments, user cancellations (1032), and failures, complete with M-Pesa receipt extraction.

    Reconciliation Worker: A scheduled background cron job (node-cron) that periodically scans stale PENDING transactions, queries Safaricom's status endpoint, and synchronizes local records.

    Spike Arrest Protection: Throttled query loops (6-second pacing delays and batch caps) to prevent Safaricom API rate-limiting (SpikeArrestViolation).

2. Business-to-Customer (B2C / Bulk Disbursement)

    Secure Payouts: Implements RSA PKCS1 v1.5 public key encryption for SecurityCredential generation using Safaricom's official developer certificate (Buffer-based reading to prevent operator account locks/Error 8006).

    Asynchronous Webhooks: Dual callback endpoints for transaction results (/api/v1/mpesa/b2c-result) and queue timeouts (/api/v1/mpesa/b2c-timeout).

    Multi-Tenant Routing: Maps internal transaction IDs (internalTxId) back to client-specific callback URLs to notify dependent microservices (e.g., Hostelix, Lernesis) upon successful fund disbursement.

📁 Project Structure
Plaintext

Backend/
├── src/
│   ├── configs/             # Environment parser & MongoDB connection setup
│   ├── Controllers/
│   │   ├── B2C_controllers/ # B2C callback and timeout handlers
│   │   └── C2B_controllers/ # STK push, payment callback & query routers
│   ├── Models/              # Mongoose schemas for transactions
│   ├── security/            # OAuth token generation & RSA B2C encryption
│   ├── services/            # Daraja API service calls & webhook dispatchers
│   ├── types/               # TypeScript interfaces and data contracts
│   ├── workers/             # Background cron reconciliation jobs
│   └── Server.js            # Express app bootstrap, helmet, CORS & graceful shutdown
├── .env                     # Environment variables
└── package.json

⚙️ Environment Variables (.env)

Create a .env file in your root directory matching the following configuration:
Code snippet

# Server Configuration
SERVER_PORT=8000
ENVIRONMENT=Development
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,https://yourdomain.com

# Database
DATABASE_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017/mpesa_gateway

# Safaricom C2B Credentials
CONSUMER_KEY=your_sandbox_consumer_key
CONSUMER_SECRET=your_sandbox_consumer_secret
SHORT_CODE=174379
PASSKEY=your_stk_passkey
STK_PUSH_URL=https://sandbox.safaricom.co.ke/mpesa/stkpush/v1/processrequest
PAYMENT_STATUS_QUERY_URL=https://sandbox.safaricom.co.ke/mpesa/stkpushquery/v1/query
URL_ACCESS_TOKEN_PARSER=https://sandbox.safaricom.co.ke/oauth/v1/generate?grant_type=client_credentials

# Safaricom B2C Credentials
B2C_INITIATOR_NAME=your_b2c_initiator_name
B2C_INITIATOR_PASSWORD=your_b2c_initiator_password
B2C_SHORT_CODE=your_b2c_shortcode
B2C_PAYOUT_URL=https://sandbox.safaricom.co.ke/mpesa/b2c/v1/paymentrequest

# Webhook URLs (Exposed via ngrok or production domain)
PAYMENT_CALLBACK_URL=https://your-domain.ngrok-free.dev/api/v1/mpesa/callback
B2C_RESULT_URL=https://your-domain.ngrok-free.dev/api/v1/mpesa/b2c-result
B2C_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_URL=https://your-domain.ngrok-free.dev/api/v1/mpesa/b2c-timeout

# Security
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_key

🛠️ Installation & Running

    Install Dependencies:
    Bash

    npm install

    Run in Development Mode (with TypeScript compilation & nodemon):
    Bash

    npm run dev

    Build for Production:
    Bash

    npm run build
    npm start

🔌 API Endpoints Reference
C2B Endpoints

    Initiate STK Push: POST /api/v1/stkpush

        Payload: { phoneNumber, amount, accountReference, internalTxId, clientCallbackUrl, serviceName }

    STK Push Callback: POST /api/v1/mpesa/callback (Called by Safaricom)

    Manual / Programmatic Query: POST /api/v1/query/payments

        Payload: { PaymentId, identifierType: "internalTxId" | "checkoutRequestID", verifiedServiceName }

B2C Endpoints

    B2C Result Callback: POST /api/v1/mpesa/b2c-result (Called by Safaricom)

    B2C Timeout Callback: POST /api/v1/mpesa/b2c-timeout (Called by Safaricom)

🔒 Security & Reliability Measures

    Incapsula Firewall Bypass: Outgoing fetch calls include standard browser headers (User-Agent, Accept: application/json) to prevent 403 HTML challenge blocks.

    Exact Optional Property Compliance: Strict TypeScript configurations (exactOptionalPropertyTypes) enforced across database models and API payloads.

    Graceful Shutdown: Intercepts SIGTERM and SIGINT signals to safely close active HTTP connections and flush database pools without dropping requests.
